						<div class="flexblocks">
        <div>
                                <span data-anchor id="id-014618a6-0"></span>
                                <div class="absatz">
                                    <div >
                                                <p>The Institute for Formal Methods of Computer Science (FMI) belongs to the <a title="IvI" href="http://www.ivi.uni-stuttgart.de/">Institutsverbund Informatik (IvI)</a> (internal only) and was spun off on 27.11.2002 from the former <a title="IFI" href="http://pcbs13.informatik.uni-stuttgart.de/ifi/ifiold.htm">Institut für Informatik (IFI)</a>.</p>
<h6>Note on enquiries for theses and study projects</h6>
<p>Requests for theses or study projects at our institute are generally welcome. However, a prerequisite for meaningful academic supervision is that you have already attended advanced courses at our institute or are familiar with our research focus areas through work as a tutor or research assistant (Hiwi).<br /><br />If your request does not indicate any relevant academic connection to our teaching offerings or research topics, we reserve the right to decline supervision; in such cases, no response should be expected.</p>
<p>Further information about research and teaching activities of the institute can be found on the sub-webpages of the individual groups below.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></div>
